18:T552,🌟 We Are Hiring – Join Our Team at Oban Hotel Lahore 🌟

Oban Hotel Lahore is expanding its professional team and we are looking for passionate, dedicated, and experienced individuals to become a part of our growing family. If you have proven expertise in the hotel industry and a commitment to excellence, we invite you to apply for the following positions:

🔹 Sales Manager – Salary 70,000 – 90,000 PKR + Fuel & Incentives
👉 Hotel line experienced is must

🔹 Pakistani Chef – Salary 45,000 – 50,000 PKR
👉 Hotel line experienced is must

🔹 Electrician – Salary 34,000 – 36,000 PKR
👉 Hotel line experienced is must

🔹 Waiters (03 Positions) – Salary 32,000 PKR + Tips
👉 Hotel line experienced is must

🔹 Asst. Restaurant Manager (ARM) – Salary 40,000 – 45,000 PKR + Tips
👉 Hotel line experienced is must

Important Notes:
✔ No Accommodation will be provided.
✔ One Meal and Two Teas will be provided daily.

📍 Location: Oban Hotel Lahore, 81 CII, Off MM Alam Road, Block C2, Gulberg III, Lahore.

📧 Email: hrm@obanhotel.pk


If you meet the criteria and are ready to excel in a professional hospitality environment, kindly share your updated CV at the given email address or contact us directly.

Be a part of Oban Hotel Lahore – Where Excellence Meets Hospitality!19:T621,Join Big Byte Insights : Empowering Fresh Graduates in Data Science!

Big Byte Insights, is excited to invite fresh graduates to kickstart their careers in data science through our paid internship program. This opportunity offers hands-on experience,mentorship, and the chance to work on impactful projects in the data science realm.

𝗪𝗵𝗼 𝗖𝗮𝗻 𝗔𝗽𝗽𝗹𝘆?
-  Fresh graduates in Computer Science, Data Science, Engineering or related fields
-  Proficiency in programming languages such as Python
-  Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with a keen eye for identifying patterns in data.
-  Familiarity with data visualization tools (e.g., Excel, Tableau, Power BI)
-  Passion for data analysis, problem-solving, and innovation
- 
𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝗪𝗲 𝗢𝗳𝗳𝗲𝗿:-
  A paid internship with a competitive stipend
-  Opportunity to work on real-world data science projects
-  Mentorship from experienced data scientists
-  Training in big data technologies and cloud computing platforms
-  Possibility of a full-time job offer based on performance
- 
𝗟𝗼𝗰𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻: Cantt, Lahore

Ready to embark on your data science journey? Apply now and become a part of our innovative team Big Byte Insights!

𝗛𝗼𝘄 𝘁𝗼 𝗔𝗽𝗽𝗹𝘆:
Send your resume to pplsuccess@bigbyte.com with the subject line "Data Science Internship Application".

Note: Candidates with a strong foundation in data science skills and who have done FYP in Data science are highly encourage to apply.1a:T4bf,🏨 Job Opportunity – Front Desk Officer (Male & Female)
 Location: Lahore
Hotel D Gates, a 4-star hospitality destination in Lahore, is seeking dynamic and well-groomed Front Desk Officers to join our team. The ideal candidates will be the first point of contact for our guests and play a vital role in creating a welcoming and professional atmosphere.
Key Responsibilities
Greet guests warmly and manage check-in/check-out procedures.
Handle reservations, calls, and guest inquiries efficiently.
Maintain guest records and ensure smooth front desk operations.
Coordinate with other departments to ensure guest satisfaction.
Uphold hotel standards of hospitality and professionalism.
Requirements
Graduate or equivalent qualification.
Excellent communication skills (English & Urdu).
Strong interpersonal and customer service skills.
Presentable personality with professional grooming.
Computer literacy (MS Office, hotel software Munshi 10 preferred).
Prior experience in hospitality will be an advantage.
Details
Position: Front Desk Officer (Male & Female)
Job Type: Full-Time
Location: Lahore
📩 Interested candidates are encouraged to apply by sending their CVs to: hr@hoteldgates.com1b:T6e1,We’re seeking an experienced "Engineering Manager" to lead our fully remote, multidisciplinary engineering team (software development, automation, data science, and web applications). In this leadership role, you’ll drive projects from concept to launch, ensuring technical excellence, scalability, and timely delivery.


Key Responsibilities:

- Lead, mentor, and manage a distributed engineering team.
- Oversee full product development lifecycles.
- Collaborate with cross-functional teams to align goals.
- Drive technical architecture, scalability, and system quality.
- Recruit, evaluate, and grow engineering talent.

Required Skills & Experience:

- 5–8 years of relevant experience (3+ years in leadership).
- Proven success in launching/managing software projects.
- Strong knowledge of NextJS, JavaScript, Python, SQL, serverless infrastructure.
- Excellent leadership, communication, and remote team management.
- Bachelor’s in CS/Engineering (Master’s preferred).

Additional Requirements (Must-Have) :

- Ability to work full PST hours (8 AM – 5 PM California time).
- Fluent English communication (spoken & written).
- A Windows or Mac computer with webcam available for daily use.
- VPN software installation on the work computer.
- Willingness to sign an NDA.
- Completion of employment verification and a comprehensive background check.
- Passing any role-related technical/aptitude assessments.

Preferred Background :

- Experience with fintech, lending, or real estate platforms.
- Exposure to data science or automation projects.
- Familiarity with Jira, Confluence, GitHub.

Applications are open only to candidates who match the above requirements. Submit your resume at hr@morfinancial.com1d:T9e7,🚀 We're Hiring: Senior React.js Developer (Remote)
📍 Location: Global / Remote
 🕒 Job Type: Full-Time
 
About MUST Company

At MUST Company, we’re building innovative, user-centric web applications that shape the future of tech. As a forward-thinking team, we thrive on creativity, collaboration, and clean code. Now, we're looking for a Senior React.js Developer to lead the charge on front-end excellence.
If you're passionate about crafting high-performance, scalable web applications using modern technologies, this is your opportunity to make a global impact—remotely.

🔧 What You’ll Do

Develop and maintain modern, high-quality web applications with React.js, Next.js, and TypeScript
Collaborate closely with design, backend, and product teams to create seamless user experiences
Implement responsive UI with Tailwind CSS for consistent, scalable design
Optimize front-end performance, scalability, and accessibility
Lead code reviews, mentor junior developers, and uphold high development standards
Stay current with the latest tech trends and advocate for best practices
Participate actively in Agile/Scrum ceremonies

✅ What You Bring

Top Skills Required:
React.js: Deep knowledge of component architecture, hooks, and state management
Next.js: Experience with SSR, static generation, and performance optimization
TypeScript: Strong understanding of type safety and scalable application structure
Tailwind CSS: Mastery in utility-first styling and responsive design
Modern front-end development experience including performance tuning, cross-browser support, and accessibility

Bonus Skills:

Experience with RESTful APIs and GraphQL
Familiarity with Jest, React Testing Library, or Cypress
Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines, Git workflows, SEO, and web accessibility standards

📚 Qualifications

5+ years of professional experience in front-end development
Proven experience delivering production-ready web applications
Strong problem-solving and debugging skills
Excellent communication and collaboration
Degree in Computer Science or related field (or equivalent experience)

🎁 What We Offer

💸 Competitive salary and benefits
🌍 100% Remote work environment
📈 Career growth & learning opportunities
👥 Collaborative and inclusive team culture
🚀 Work on exciting, real-world projects with a passionate team.

📩 Ready to Join Us?
If this sounds like the role for you, we want to hear from you!
 Send your resume to b.sara@mufin.co.kr1e:T466,🌟 We’re Hiring: Part-Time Bookkeeper 🌟
📍 Location: Remote - Pakistan

 🕒 Schedule: 25 hours per week (Fixed EST hours)
We are looking for a detail-oriented and dependable Bookkeeper to join our team. If you are organized, efficient, and thrive in a structured part-time role, this could be the perfect fit for you.

🔑 Responsibilities:
- Record and maintain daily financial transactions
- Manage Accounts Payable and Accounts Receivable
- Handle intercompany transactions
- Perform bank and credit card reconciliations
- Support payroll processing and entries
- Assist with month-end close and prepare timely monthly reports
- Ensure accuracy and compliance in all financial records

✅ Requirements:
- Bachelor’s degree in Accounting/Finance (preferred)
- 4+ years of bookkeeping experience
- Proficiency with QuickBooks (or similar accounting software)
- Strong Microsoft Excel skills
- Excellent attention to detail and organizational skills
- Ability to work independently and meet deadlines
- Strong communication skills

📩 How to Apply:
